# Sloth OS: Num Lock is on from the start, so the number pad works right away (GitHub issue #17: a PIN of digits,
# and Num Lock was off at every start). KWin sets it when it starts (0 = on, 1 = off, 2 = leave it as it is): on the
# login screen too, which runs KWin as well (Plasma Login Manager). The user can still change it in System Settings
# → Keyboard (that goes to ~/.config/kcminputrc).
[Keyboard]
NumLock=0
